<title>PERU: Credicorp's 1996 net rises 11.4 percent.</title>
<headline>Credicorp's 1996 net rises 11.4 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Q4:</p>
<p>Shr $0.425 vs $0.522</p>
<p>Net $26.1 million vs $32.0 million</p>
<p>Revs $85.5 million vs $80.9 million</p>
<p>Year</p>
<p>Shr $1.894 vs $1.699</p>
<p>Net $116.1 million vs $104.2 million</p>
<p>Revs $318.9 million vs $261.7 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Credicorp Ltd is a holding company that began operating in October 1995, so comparatives are an estimate based on its subsidiaries' results.</p>
<p>Credicorp is Peru's largest provider of financial services and owns 90.1 percent of Peru's largest full-service bank, Banco de Credito.</p>
<p>((--Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom 511-221-2134))</p>
</text>
